 "turns": [
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hi, how are things with you?",
   "est_sec": 1.96,
   "gap_before": 0.63,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_11"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Pretty relaxed today.",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 0.92,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_22"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Why do coffees from different countries taste so different? I thought coffee was coffee.",
   "est_sec": 4.44,
   "gap_before": 0.22,
   "block": "coffee.dlg22",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "It's a bit like wine. The type of plant, the soil, the altitude and the climate all shape the flavour.",
   "est_sec": 6.3,
   "gap_before": 0.49,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "coffee.dlg22"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "So what does Ethiopian taste like compared to, say, Brazilian?",
   "est_sec": 3.2,
   "gap_before": 1.28,
   "block": "coffee.dlg22",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Ethiopian coffees are often bright and fruity, sometimes floral. Brazilian ones tend to be nutty and chocolatey, with less acidity.",
   "est_sec": 6.3,
   "gap_before": 1.03,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "coffee.dlg22"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Do you reckon, Arjun, that Moshi can tell when I'm grumpy?",
   "est_sec": 3.51,
   "gap_before": 1.44,
   "block": "mm_093",
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "moshi_mention",
   "phrasing": "mm_093",
   "name_pos": "middle",
   "addressee": "Arjun"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "And Colombian?",
   "est_sec": 0.72,
   "gap_before": 2.65,
   "block": "coffee.dlg22",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Usually balanced, a little sweet, medium body. Many people find it a great everyday coffee.",
   "est_sec": 4.75,
   "gap_before": 0.35,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "coffee.dlg22"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Does how it's processed",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 0.45,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "coffee.dlg22"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "matter too?",
   "est_sec": 0.72,
   "gap_before": 2.74,
   "block": "coffee.dlg22",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hugely. Natural process coffees, dried with the fruit still on, taste fruitier. Washed coffees taste cleaner and crisper.",
   "est_sec": 5.68,
   "gap_before": 1.12,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "coffee.dlg22"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Hold on, really?",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 0.47,
   "block": "coffee.dlg22",
   "kind": "wait_like",
   "phrasing": "waitlike_11",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "I'm fairly sure about it, but I could be wrong. What sounds off to you?",
   "est_sec": 4.75,
   "gap_before": 1.02,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "coffee.dlg22"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I should do a tasting at home.",
   "est_sec": 2.27,
   "gap_before": 1.03,
   "block": "coffee.dlg22",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "That's a fun idea. Brew a few side by side the same way, and you'll really notice the differences.",
   "est_sec": 5.99,
   "gap_before": 1.06,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "coffee.dlg22"
  }
 ]
}
